Interactive USD edits of arnold light groups mixed with UsdLux light linking, with the usd procedural cache_id and with the render delegate

see #2835

Three grey spheres are lit by a red, a green and a blue distant light, linked with UsdLux light link collections,
while the left sphere has an arnold light group (primvars:arnold:use_light_group / primvars:arnold:light_group,
holding arnold node names) that takes precedence over them. A mesh light authored with primvars:arnold:light is in
the scene, as C4DtoA authors them. Lights are added to and removed from the arnold light groups, an arnold light
group is added to the center sphere and removed, the collections are edited, and the lights in the arnold light
group, the mesh light and the spheres are deleted. The stage is re-rendered after each edit.
The scenario runs with the "usd" procedural reading the stage through its cache_id in an interactive render session,
and with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the procedural render of step 6
(the edited collections) is compared against the reference image. The legacy reader isn't run, it hangs when a light
is removed (as in test_2343.8), test_2835.2 covers it.

author: cyril.pichard

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
